------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party engine dependency
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pw-planner is a UI shell. All quantitative computation is performed by the
nexus-core planning engine (separate repository, Apache-2.0), which in turn
relies on QuantLib, FinancePy, Zipline-Reloaded, Alphalens, NumPy, and SciPy.
See nexus-core's NOTICE for those attributions. pw-planner ships none of that
code; it communicates with the engine over the network.

This open-source repo is demo / case-study tooling and carries only a
lightweight structural PII tripwire. Production compliance (real PII
de-identification, books-and-records audit logging) and any pw-api integration
are out of scope here; they live in a private deployment that integrates
pwos-core. Use this software with de-identified or fake client data only.

